Correction from a live run (my earlier note was wrong): SAM 3.1 rejects a bare [input_text, input_image] list with
`400 input[0] did not match any supported type`. The accepted shape wraps the parts in one user message:
  input=[{"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "input_text", "text": "<concept or object prompt>"},
                                      {"type": "input_image", "image_url": "data:image/jpeg;base64,..."}]}]
(`{"type": "message", "role": "user", "content": [...]}` also works). Verified live just now: concept "battery" on
engine_bay_02.jpg streams `<0f>0<|box;x1=963;y1=690;x2=1130;y2=830;w=1280;h=960|><|mask;...|>`.

Fix backend/mmc/meta/sam.py (image path, and make the video path at ~line 421 use the same user-message wrapper with
its file/video part), update the docstrings and the docs/DECISIONS.md M5-reconciled entry, and add a unit test that
asserts the request `input` is a single user message containing input_text then input_image. Keep the captured stream
fixtures as they are. Run cd backend && uv run pytest -q (or .venv python) until green. Do not commit. Finish with
files changed and the test count.
